    "frames": [
      {
        "slide": 1,
        "role": "cover",
        "subject": "The finished 6061 housing part sits in the vise on the cast iron T-slot table. It has two pockets with shadowed walls and four counterbored bosses. Above it the fluted end mill in its knurled holder is held clear between two coolant hoses, all under the dark spindle head that carries the type.",
        "visual_consequence": "A finished aluminium part sits in an open machine with the cutter held off the work. The reader sees what the plant makes, and that the machine is waiting, before reading any number.",
        "weakness": "The artwork is unchanged; only the type changed. The two-line hook ends inside the counter's right margin, and the spindle head's diagonal seam runs behind 'expected in early 2027', dark on dark at no cost to contrast. 'Drawn to illustrate.' sits alone on the dek's fourth line. Every chip is the same flat faceted C ring rather than a curled chip, one sits under 'c34', and a small blue-white rectangle remains behind the vise handle. Neither blocks the frame. No missile is drawn.",
        "repair": "Optional polish: replace the planar C rings with curled helical chips of varied size and twist, and keep them out of the area around the 'c3 c4 c7 c34' line.",
        "encoding_reads": true,
        "dominant_subject_finished": true,
        "feed_legible": true,
        "inputs": {
