      {
        "slide": 6,
        "role": "evidence",
        "subject": "Seen from a steep aerial, 100 machining centres in ten columns of ten, each with a dark enclosure roof, a pale spindle column cap standing proud at the rear, a round tool drum hood on its west side, a pendant, a stack pole and a front face with door windows. Across a dark aisle at lower right, a grey apron carries Hadrian's 24 as empty satin pads in cyan tape outlines, six rows of four, each with four levelling plates.",
        "visual_consequence": "Without the headline a reader sees a large, dense block of distinct machines and, set apart at the same pitch, a small closed block of cyan outlines with nothing standing in them. The 24 read as planned and not yet there, beside a plant that is already full.",
        "weakness": "Minor only. One pad, the second bay of the bottom row, still shows a fine horizontal hatch. The bottom-left machine's drum hood is cut by the left edge though its body is in frame. The near white column caps are the brightest values and compete a little with the cyan. The floor above the bays is near black with faint streaks. All 24 outlines close inside the frame and the footer sits on bare floor.",
        "repair": "none required",
