      {
        "slide": 9,
        "role": "close",
        "subject": "The cell's empty bays at standing eye height: satin pads in cyan tape outlines with levelling plates, receding in rows across dark aisles. A machinist in a hard hat stands inside a bay two rows back. Along the east wall at right stand four of Lockheed's graphite enclosures with door windows, handles, pendants on arms and stack lights. No drop cord crosses the type.",
        "visual_consequence": "The cell is still only tape and plates on an empty floor. Lockheed's own machines already stand beside it, and a Lockheed worker is standing in it. Who runs it, and that it doesn't exist yet, both read without the dek.",
        "weakness": "Minor only. The near pads read as matte grey speckled concrete with a soft falloff and no sheen of the tape or plates. The four machines' windows are flat pale blue-grey, not lit. A tall steel post beside the foreground plate has no evident job. The fourth machine is cut by the right edge.",
